{
  "$comment": "EDE-8 (eDE M0, 2026-11-05): THE SURFACE HEADER AND THE TIER C RULES. Every shell document (a person's ~/.config/ede/ui/<name>.json, the factory copy in /usr/share/ede/ui) is a genUI document ({catalogId?, root | components, data?}) plus a `surface` object that tells ede-shell how the document sits on the screen. normalizeSurface(header) fills the defaults and returns the header, or the issues that refuse it; one issue refuses the whole document (apply.json). A LAYER surface: `layer` background|bottom|top|overlay (default top; the wlr-layer-shell layer); `anchor` = the screen edges it sticks to, a list of top|bottom|left|right (default none = centred; each edge at most once); `size` = {width?, height?} in logical px, whole and positive, and an axis stretched between two opposite anchors (left+right, top+bottom) needs none while any other axis MUST have one; `exclusiveZone` = the px other windows keep clear along the anchored edge, 0 = none (default), positive only with at least one anchored edge; `margin` = {top, right, bottom, left} px (default 0, never negative); `keyboard` none|on-demand|exclusive (default none; `exclusive` only on the top and overlay layers, as the protocol says). `onDemand` true|false (default false): a layer surface the shell opens only when asked (a hotkey, a host function: the Alt+Tab switcher, the OSD) and closes again, never at start; a popup is on demand by nature and carries no such key. A POPUP surface: `popup` = {parent: the document name it belongs to, anchor: a component id in the parent, placement bottom-start|bottom-end|top-start|top-end|left-start|right-start (default bottom-start), size: {width, height} REQUIRED} drawn as an xdg_popup of the parent's surface (gpui WindowKind::AnchoredPopup), so a menu can leave the parent's box; a popup header carries no layer, anchor, exclusiveZone, margin, keyboard or onDemand. `functions` = the host functions this document may call (default none). Unknown keys are refused. TIER C RULES (documentIssues(document)): a document grants no privileges, so a shell document (1) must be an object with `surface` and exactly one of `root` (a nested tree) or `components` (A2UI's flat list), plus only $schema, $comment, catalogId, data; (2) never holds a password field: an Input whose `type` prop (under `props` in the nested form, at the top level in the flat form) is `password` is refused by its id (a sealed Tier B surface asks for passwords); (3) may only call the host functions in surface.functions: an on.<event>.functionCall whose call is not listed is refused by its id; (4) uses ids once. These checks are structural and pure; eui-core's reducer (unknown components, props, styles, tokens, limits) runs after them in the Rust runtime and the same issue rule applies.",
